tps://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137117035?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss","html_url":"https://github.com/Thiago-Weiss","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-20T14:31:04Z","updated_at":"2026-07-20T14:35:43Z","body":"> It fixes the same issue as #120517, no?\r\n\r\nYes, but there’s a difference in approach: approach #120517 checks if the object has changed to avoid rebuilding the `inspector`, whereas my approach always rebuilds it, saves the state, and reapplies it afterward. Because of this, my approach ensures the previous state is reapplied even if the object changes; so, if a tile changes, it rebuilds but preserves the visual state, whereas the other one doesn't preserve the visual state.\r\n\r\nvideo showing the two approaches\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a4d9dbad-e462-4db9-b491-cd35ae644bee\r\n\r\nPS: My approach still has a small problem: when the object is changed, it doesn't update the scroll, which is strange because when it rebuilds using the same object, it updates. Can anyone help me with this? I just want to use `await get_tree().process_frame` and then update the value.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5023409158/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5024105765","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121561#issuecomment-5024105765","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121561","id":5024105765,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABK3XFJQ","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-20T15:38:27Z","updated_at":"2026-07-20T15:38:27Z","body":"I guess both PRs can be merged then, but this one is more a usability enhancement.\r\n\r\n> I just want to use await get_tree().process_frame and then update the value.\r\n\r\nYou can connect to `process_frame` with `CONNECT_ONESHOT`, but that shouldn't be really necessary.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5024105765/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5024415456","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121561#issuecomment-5024415456","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121561","id":5024415456,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABK3p-4A","user":{"login":"Thiago-Weiss","id":137117035,"node_id":"U_kgDOCCw9aw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137117035?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss","html_url":"https://github.com/Thiago-Weiss","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Thiago-Weiss/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-20T16:10:30Z","updated_at":"2026-07-20T16:10:30Z","body":"> I guess both PRs can be merged then, but this one is more a usability enhancement.\r\n\r\nI agree, because there's no need to keep rebuilding the `inspector` constantly and when the object changes and the `inspector` is rebuilt it will still maintain the same state. To improve the integration should I copy the other PR and integrate it into this one?\r\n\r\n> You can connect to `process_frame` with `CONNECT_ONESHOT`, but that shouldn't be really necessary.\r\n\r\nI tried all 3 and it doesn't work when the object is swapped.\r\n\r\n\t\t\t//get_tree()->connect(SNAME(\"process_frame\"), callable_mp(tile_inspector, &EditorInspector::set_scroll_offset).bind(scroll_offset), CONNECT_ONE_SHOT);\r\n\t\t\t//get_tree()->connect(SNAME(\"process_frame\"), callable_mp(tile_inspector, &EditorInspector::set_scroll_offset).bind(scroll_offset), CONNECT_ONE_SHOT | CONNECT_DEFERRED);\r\n\t\t\t//callable_mp(tile_inspector, &EditorInspector::set_scroll_offset).call_deferred(scroll_offset);","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5024415456/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]